      "note": "Inspected owner-supplied cararayan-national-high-school.png on 2026-10-08; capture date unknown. URL locates the site. Two large distinguishable interior canopy groups west of open concrete yard, perimeter belts along north/west/east/south and central small green pockets. Actual exposed yard is bounded by classroom roofs and planted islands. No broad lawn/hedge visible. Ignore map operating-status text; no furniture inferred from tiny courtyard objects. Large northeast classroom, west/top classroom chain and isolated central-east roof enclose a concrete court/yard. Ignore unverified operating-status label. Independent excluded check errors: 1.68 m, 3.31 m. Visible crown centers are fitted to clear trunks within the observed crown footprint (maximum seven metres); crowns may overhang roofs and roads. Crown widths in the dense belts are estimated from image pixels against their matched local roof scale; existing circular crowns approximate irregular/elliptical image crowns. Complete mapped roofs, pitches, full-width paths/roads, water and farmland remain unchanged. Planted islands take precedence over exposed paving; ground under opaque canopy is not invented. No surveyed boundary, species, construction date or exact inventory inferred; no bitmap ships."
